{
  "base_commit": "9348fa4dcd108be8f537568d0a60f3b41ce15c71",
  "branch": "agent/v19-unverified-is-not-true",
  "caveats": [
    "`--check` does not protect the committed artefacts: main() rebuilds OUT before check_determinism diffs it, so under a mutation it compares mutated against mutated. The 35 committed artefacts are pinned by git diff and human attention only. (determinism_sandbox.py:12-16 recorded this for V16.)",
    "core/reversibility.py: 90 of 218 published claims (41.3%) are `deferred` or `unreachable` and neither class can reach the build gate; all 35/35 worlds carry at least one. Registered, not fixed - see INBOX-PROPOSAL-20260729-*.md in this directory.",
    "37 rules self-exempt from `declared_never_fires` via `cascade: True` / `clause: True`, declared by the rule and independently checked by nobody. Same proposal."
  ],
  "cell": "V19",
